From 2d16e38768bd297f816e4eeafac62d4d2bcabc6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:03:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Finish the jest-to-vitest sweep the first pass missed

The first sweep matched \bjest\.(fn|spyOn|...) on a single line, but the
formatter had broken several call sites across two - `getValueSpy = jest`
then `.spyOn(...)` on the next line - so those survived untouched while the
type annotation beside them was rewritten to MockInstance. The two then
disagreed and tsc reported it; four files were affected.

Also imports vi, describe, it and expect where they were still being used
as globals. apps/web sets globals: false, so a test relying on them does
not fail an assertion - it fails to load.

Fork-Feature: fork-tooling
